WEBVTT

00:00.352 --> 00:01.921
- [Voiceover] So we have a
nice little equation here

00:01.921 --> 00:03.612
dealing with rational expressions.

00:03.612 --> 00:05.242
And I encourage you to pause the video

00:05.242 --> 00:07.988
and see if you can figure
out what values of x

00:07.988 --> 00:10.947
satisfy this equation.

00:10.947 --> 00:12.637
Alright, let's work through this together.

00:12.637 --> 00:14.690
So the first thing I'd like to do

00:14.690 --> 00:16.803
is just see if I can simplify this at all,

00:16.803 --> 00:19.278
and maybe by finding some common factors

00:19.278 --> 00:21.028
between numerators and denominators,

00:21.028 --> 00:23.956
or common factors on either
side of the equal sign.

00:23.956 --> 00:27.850
So let's factor all of the
numerators and the denominators.

00:27.850 --> 00:30.144
All the ones on the right-hand
side are already done.

00:30.144 --> 00:31.925
So this thing up here,

00:31.925 --> 00:34.370
I could rewrite this as, let's see.

00:34.370 --> 00:36.845
What's product is 21?

00:36.845 --> 00:38.958
What two numbers, when I
take their product, is 21?

00:38.958 --> 00:41.252
Positive 21, so they're
going to have the same sign.

00:41.252 --> 00:43.959
And when I add them, I get negative 10.

00:43.959 --> 00:45.438
Well, negative seven and negative three,

00:45.438 --> 00:46.434
so this could be rewritten

00:46.434 --> 00:51.022
as x minus seven times x minus three.

00:51.022 --> 00:53.005
This over here, both
are divisible by three.

00:53.005 --> 00:57.382
I could rewrite this as
three times x minus four.

00:57.382 --> 00:59.072
And these are already factored.

00:59.072 --> 01:01.085
So the one thing that
jumps out at me is I have

01:01.085 --> 01:05.060
x minus four in the denominator
on the left-hand side

01:05.060 --> 01:07.505
and on the right-hand side.

01:07.505 --> 01:11.067
And so, if I were to multiply
both sides by x minus four.

01:11.067 --> 01:12.788
So actually, let me just...

01:12.788 --> 01:16.470
Let me formally replace this with that.

01:16.470 --> 01:18.613
And up here, it's not so obvious

01:18.613 --> 01:20.002
that it's going to be valuable for me

01:20.002 --> 01:21.451
to keep this factored form.

01:21.451 --> 01:23.775
So I'm just going to keep
it in this yellow form.

01:23.775 --> 01:26.231
In the expanded out form.

01:26.231 --> 01:28.796
So let me just scratch that out for now,

01:28.796 --> 01:30.275
because once I,

01:30.275 --> 01:32.178
well, let me multiply by x minus four.

01:32.178 --> 01:35.438
So, if we multiply both
sides by x minus four,

01:35.438 --> 01:36.826
and once again, why am I doing this?

01:36.826 --> 01:39.935
Just so I get rid of the x
minus four in the denominators.

01:39.935 --> 01:44.855
x minus four, and then x minus four.

01:44.855 --> 01:47.059
That and that cancels.

01:47.059 --> 01:48.811
That and that cancels,

01:48.811 --> 01:50.773
and then we're left
with, in the numerator,

01:50.773 --> 01:55.773
we're left with our x
squared minus 10 x plus 21,

01:57.686 --> 02:00.976
and, let's see, divided by three.

02:00.976 --> 02:03.572
Divided by three

02:03.572 --> 02:07.133
is equal to x minus five.

02:07.133 --> 02:08.703
Let's see, now, what we can do,

02:08.703 --> 02:10.333
and actually I could have
done it in the last step,

02:10.333 --> 02:13.835
is I can multiply both sides by three.

02:13.835 --> 02:15.525
Multiply both sides.

02:15.525 --> 02:16.551
Do that in another color

02:16.551 --> 02:18.755
just so it sticks out a little more.

02:18.755 --> 02:22.830
So I can multiply both sides by three.

02:22.830 --> 02:26.392
So multiply both sides by three.

02:26.392 --> 02:28.957
On the left-hand side,
that and that cancels,

02:28.957 --> 02:33.957
and I'll just be left with x
squared minus 10 x plus 21,

02:35.538 --> 02:37.409
and on, and I don't have
a denominator any more.

02:37.409 --> 02:39.824
My denominator is one, so
I don't need to write it.

02:39.824 --> 02:41.757
Is going to be equal to three times,

02:41.757 --> 02:43.719
let's just distribute the three.

02:43.719 --> 02:45.803
Three times x is three x.

02:45.803 --> 02:50.089
Three times negative five is negative 15.

02:50.089 --> 02:52.223
And now I can get this into
standard quadratic form

02:52.223 --> 02:55.000
by getting all of these terms
onto the left-hand side.

02:55.000 --> 02:56.701
The best way to do that,

02:56.701 --> 02:59.026
let's subtract three x from the right,

02:59.026 --> 03:00.112
but I can't just do it from the right

03:00.112 --> 03:01.531
otherwise the equality won't held.

03:01.531 --> 03:04.217
I have to do it from both sides
if I want equality to hold.

03:04.217 --> 03:07.055
And, I want to get rid
of this negative 15,

03:07.055 --> 03:09.460
so I can add 15 to both sides.

03:09.460 --> 03:11.825
So, let's do that.

03:11.825 --> 03:14.692
And what we are left with,
scroll down a little bit,

03:14.692 --> 03:17.270
so let's have a little more space.

03:17.270 --> 03:19.232
What we are going to be left with

03:19.232 --> 03:24.083
is x squared minus 13 x

03:25.071 --> 03:26.304
and then plus,

03:26.304 --> 03:30.828
what is this, plus 36.

03:30.828 --> 03:33.603
Plus 36. Did I do that right?

03:33.603 --> 03:35.625
Yep, plus 36

03:35.625 --> 03:40.472
is equal to, is equal to zero.

03:42.004 --> 03:43.944
Alright, now let's see,
we have it as a quadratic

03:43.944 --> 03:45.211
in the standard form.

03:45.211 --> 03:46.695
How can we solve this?

03:46.695 --> 03:48.023
So first thing, can we factor this.

03:48.023 --> 03:50.196
Product of two numbers, 36.

03:50.196 --> 03:51.705
If I add them, I get negative 13.

03:51.705 --> 03:52.943
They're both going to be negative,

03:52.943 --> 03:54.041
since they have to have the same sign

03:54.041 --> 03:56.486
to get their product to be positive.

03:56.486 --> 03:59.866
And, let's see, nine and
four seem to do the trick.

03:59.866 --> 04:02.070
So, or negative nine and negative four.

04:02.070 --> 04:06.386
So, x minus four times x minus nine

04:06.386 --> 04:08.278
is equal to zero.

04:08.278 --> 04:09.274
Well, that's going to happen

04:09.274 --> 04:13.834
if either x minus four is equal to zero or

04:13.834 --> 04:17.656
x minus nine is equal to zero.

04:17.656 --> 04:19.256
We'll add four to both sides of this.

04:19.256 --> 04:21.852
This happens when x is equal to four.

04:21.852 --> 04:23.211
Add nine to both side of this.

04:23.211 --> 04:25.938
This happens when x is equal to nine.

04:25.938 --> 04:27.709
So we could say that the solutions are

04:27.709 --> 04:30.909
x equals four or x equals nine.

04:30.909 --> 04:35.909
So, x is equal to four, or x equals nine.

04:36.161 --> 04:37.821
But we need to be careful.

04:37.821 --> 04:38.968
Because we have to remember,

04:38.968 --> 04:40.538
in our original expression,

04:40.538 --> 04:43.647
x minus four was a factor
of both denominators.

04:43.647 --> 04:45.216
And so if we actually try to test

04:45.216 --> 04:47.208
x minus four in the original equation,

04:47.208 --> 04:48.506
not one of these intermediary steps,

04:48.506 --> 04:50.806
the original equation, I would end up

04:50.806 --> 04:52.805
dividing by zero right over here,

04:52.805 --> 04:56.147
and actually, I'd end up by
zero right over there as well.

04:56.147 --> 04:58.099
So the original equations, if
I tried to substitute four,

04:58.099 --> 04:59.850
they don't make sense.

04:59.850 --> 05:01.993
So this is actually an
extraneous solution.

05:01.993 --> 05:04.891
It's not going to be a solution
to the original equation.

05:04.891 --> 05:09.459
The only solution is x is equal to 9.
